# Copy this file to your Umbrel at EXACTLY this name and location:
#   ~/umbrel/app-data/brandonjamesmarshall-transmission/.env
# It MUST be named ".env" (leading dot) and sit directly in the app folder
# — NOT in a data/ subfolder. gluetun and the mam-seedbox sidecar read it
# via the env_file directive in docker-compose.yml. Do NOT commit real
# values.
#
# Generate a WireGuard keypair locally:
#   brew install wireguard-tools          # on Mac (or apt-get install -y wireguard-tools on Linux)
#   wg genkey | tee >(wg pubkey > pub.key) > priv.key
# Paste the PUBLIC key into your iVPN account area (https://www.ivpn.net/account)
# under WireGuard, and iVPN will return your assigned tunnel address.

VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom
VPN_TYPE=wireguard

# Your 44-char base64 private key (the value of `cat priv.key`)
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=replace-with-your-private-key

# The address iVPN assigned (e.g. 172.28.135.212/32) — include the /32
WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=replace-with-your-assigned-ip/32

# --- Pin ONE iVPN server via a CUSTOM WireGuard endpoint ---
# MAM Rule 1.2 needs a SEMI-STABLE exit IP (changes less than once/hour); an
# unstable IP triggers "Unrecognized host/passkey" and MAM auto-disabling
# tracker access. We get that by pinning ONE server.
#
# We pin with a CUSTOM endpoint (VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom, above) instead of
# the `ivpn` provider + a SERVER_HOSTNAMES/SERVER_CITIES filter, because:
#   - SERVER_CITIES=Zurich ROTATES across iVPN's three Zurich servers, which
#     span two ASNs / three IP blocks (ch1=M247 185.212.170.x, ch2=Privatelayer
#     81.17.24.x, ch3=Privatelayer 141.255.166.x) — the exact IP flapping MAM
#     punishes; and
#   - gluetun's BAKED-IN server list goes stale: iVPN re-IPs servers (it moved
#     ch1 from Privatelayer 141.255.x to M247 185.212.170.x in 2026), so a
#     pinned hostname can map to a DEAD endpoint and gluetun loops forever on
#     "healthcheck i/o timeout".
# A custom endpoint pins the live server IP + key directly, entirely in this
# .env — immune to gluetun's stale list, nothing written into umbrel app-data.
#
# Default below = ch1.wg.ivpn.net (Zurich, M247). These server values are PUBLIC
# and shared by all iVPN users — only your two keys above (private key +
# assigned address) are yours. ENDPOINT_IP must be a literal IP; gluetun's
# custom mode does not resolve hostnames.
#
# TWO DIFFERENT IPs (this trips people up): WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP below
# (185.212.170.141) is the server's WireGuard LISTEN address that gluetun
# connects TO. Your EXIT IP — 185.212.170.142, the public IP trackers/MAM see,
# and the value that goes in the MAM seedbox session's "IP" field — is NAT'd
# behind it. They are SUPPOSED to differ; do NOT put the endpoint IP in MAM.
WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP=185.212.170.141
WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_PORT=2049
WIREGUARD_PUBLIC_KEY=dU7gLfcupYd37LW0q6cxC6PHMba+eUFAUOoU/ryXZkY=
#
# Failover — swap ALL THREE values above if ch1 is down/retired. Current Zurich
# servers (iVPN re-IPs/re-keys, so re-check before relying on these):
#   ch2.wg.ivpn.net  81.17.24.165     KRKeAFMJY6OH9RABaeC4feQG/JgbacZVg/w6VUjBSVQ=
#   ch3.wg.ivpn.net  141.255.166.198  JBpgBKtqIneRuEga7mbP2PAk/e4HPRaC11H0A0+R3lA=
# Re-fetch any server's live key, and dig its hostname for the current IP:
#   curl -fsS https://api.ivpn.net/v4/servers/stats \
#     | jq -r '.servers[]|select(.city=="Zurich")|"\(.hostnames.wireguard) \(.isp) \(.wg_public_key)"'
#   dig +short ch1.wg.ivpn.net        # -> WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP
# iVPN P2P-allowed list:
# https://www.ivpn.net/knowledgebase/general/which-vpn-servers-can-i-use-for-p2p-torrent-traffic/

# Optional:
# LOG_LEVEL=debug
# DOT_PROVIDERS=cloudflare,quad9

# Note: Transmission's RPC username/password are set via the USER and PASS
# env vars in docker-compose.yml (defaults: umbrel / umbrelmedia, surfaced
# in umbrelOS's app card). Edit the compose to change them.

# --- MyAnonaMouse dynamic seedbox (optional) ---
# Create a DEDICATED seedbox session at MAM -> Preferences -> Security:
#   * IP vs ASN locked = IP   (NOT ASN — iVPN spans M247 + Privatelayer ASNs, so
#     an ASN-locked session rejects with {"Success":false,"msg":"Invalid session
#     - ASN mismatch"} the moment your exit ASN differs from the locked one)
#   * Allow Session to set Dynamic Seedbox = Yes
#   * IP = your iVPN EXIT IP (e.g. 185.212.170.142), NOT your home/browser IP
#   * Label it (e.g. "umbrel transmission seedbox") so cleanup doesn't confuse it
#     with your Prowlarr session
# Paste that session's mam_id below. The mam-seedbox sidecar then (re)authorizes
# the exit IP via the Dynamic Seedbox API (max 1 update/hour) — mostly insurance
# now that the IP is pinned, but it covers NAT-pool shifts and future ch1
# re-IPs. Leave blank if you don't use MAM.
#
# Keep exactly TWO MAM sessions and prune the rest: this seedbox one (last-seen
# = iVPN IP) and your Prowlarr indexer session (last-seen = home IP). Do NOT
# delete the Prowlarr session — it's ASN-locked to your home ASN and feeds the
# indexer.
#
# ALSO register the VPN provider on your account (separate from the seedbox
# session). MAM Rule 1.2 + the 2026-06 enforcement require you to declare you use
# a VPN, or you risk being disabled for sharing iVPN's exit IP with other
# members. Check User Profile -> VPN: it should read "VPN Registration
# Confirmed"; if "Not Registered/Authorized", open a Staff ticket to register
# provider = iVPN.
MAM_ID=
